    "content": "[{\"sha\":\"ca1ea88ebf58018f40ca700a3359b6f337cfbce1\",\"node_id\":\"C_kwDOAD4oLNoAKGNhMWVhODhlYmY1ODAxOGY0MGNhNzAwYTMzNTliNmYzMzdjZmJjZTE\",\"commit\":{\"author\":{\"name\":\"Yukihiro \\\"Matz\\\" Matsumoto\",\"email\":\"matz@ruby.or.jp\",\"date\":\"2026-06-21T02:03:01Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"Yukihiro \\\"Matz\\\" Matsumoto\",\"email\":\"matz@ruby.or.jp\",\"date\":\"2026-06-22T04:41:19Z\"},\"message\":\"build: make Prism the default compiler, keep lrama as an option\\n\\nSwap the canonical gem names so a default build uses the Prism compiler\\nand tools: the Prism gems take the names mruby-compiler, mruby-eval, and\\nmruby-bin-{mrbc,mruby,mirb}, while the legacy lrama-based gems are\\nretained under a -lrama suffix for memory-constrained targets that opt\\nin. The two compilers conflict, so only one is ever present in a build.\\n\\nSupporting changes so the full default gembox builds with Prism:\\n- define global_mrb (the Prism allocator's mrb_state) in the compiler\\n  library so every executable linking libmruby resolves it, not only the\\n  mrbc/mruby/mirb front-ends; the tools now declare it extern.\\n- provide mrb_decode_insn from the Prism compiler (used by mrdb).\\n- copy node-owned (unescaped) symbol bytes into pool-owned memory in\\n  nsym so a dumped irep keeps valid symbol names after the AST is freed.\\n- rename the gem_init/final entry points to match the new gem names.\\n- bootstrap mrbc with the matching compiler; resolve mrbcfile/installer\\n  for both name sets.\\n- full-core excludes -lrama instead of -prism; the CI Prism safety-net\\n  job becomes an lrama job (build_config/lrama.rb, mrbgems/lrama.gembox).\\n- point the console build configs at mruby-compiler-lrama.\\n- update the mrdb syntax-error bintest to the Prism diagnostic format.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"tree\":{\"sha\":\"58c65a8162e3a4c81410f16ee7b7cb880d6abdbe\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/mruby/mruby/git/trees/58c65a8162e3a4c81410f16ee7b7cb880d6abdbe\"},\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/mruby/mruby/git/commits/ca1ea88ebf58018f40ca700a3359b6f337cfbce1\",\"comment_count\":0,\"verification\":{\"verified\":true,\"reason\":\"valid\",\"signature\":\"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\\n\\niF0EABECAB0WIQQjejz276bPDxKN3p04/gJpOPlJlwUCaji87wAKCRA4/gJpOPlJ\\nl3wzAJ9Sxu89qJtMtgrXsKJ1OAPgMprHCQCcDn7edCPvOpHPOvUuuKf0lJR8Ctc=\\n=/rDi\\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\",\"payload\":\"tree 58c65a8162e3a4c81410f16ee7b7cb880d6abdbe\\nparent 59b1786343054c8841fb3c7dd0af52d5067df0f9\\nauthor Yukihiro \\\"Matz\\\" Matsumoto <matz@ruby.or.jp> 1782007381 +0900\\ncommitter Yukihiro \\\"Matz\\\" Matsumoto <matz@ruby.or.jp> 1782103279 +0900\\n\\nbuild: make Prism the default compiler, keep lrama as an option\\n\\nSwap the canonical gem names so a default build uses the Prism compiler\\nand tools: the Prism gems take the names mruby-compiler, mruby-eval, and\\nmruby-bin-{mrbc,mruby,mirb}, while the legacy lrama-based gems are\\nretained under a -lrama suffix for memory-constrained targets that opt\\nin. The two compilers conflict, so only one is ever present in a build.\\n\\nSupporting changes so the full default gembox builds with Prism:\\n- define global_mrb (the Prism allocator's mrb_state) in the compiler\\n  library so every executable linking libmruby resolves it, not only the\\n  mrbc/mruby/mirb front-ends; the tools now declare it extern.\\n- provide mrb_decode_insn from the Prism compiler (used by mrdb).\\n- copy node-owned (unescaped) symbol bytes into pool-owned memory in\\n  nsym so a dumped irep keeps valid symbol names after the AST is freed.\\n- rename the gem_init/final entry points to match the new gem names.\\n- bootstrap mrbc with the matching compiler; resolve mrbcfile/installer\\n  for both name sets.\\n- full-core excludes -lrama instead of -prism; the CI Prism safety-net\\n  job becomes an lrama job (build_config/lrama.rb, mrbgems/lrama.gembox).\\n- point the console build configs at mruby-compiler-lrama.\\n- update the mrdb syntax-error bintest to the Prism diagnostic format.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\",\"verified_at\":\"202",
